2026-10-25T02:37:01.5169690Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5198020Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5200880Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5202180Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5202990Z 
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5203440Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5205920Z 
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5210300Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5210760Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5211030Z 
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5211200Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5211480Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5211710Z 
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5212150Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T02:37:01.5217450Z   $ sh ./install-nix
